infographic compare-binary-horizontal-underline-text-vs
data
  title Renaming one signature, 23 call sites
  desc Plain JS leans on grep-and-pray and fails in prod; TypeScript runs a whole-program proof that catches every stale site
  compares
    - label Plain JavaScript
      children
        - label grep + fix by hand
          desc You search call sites yourself; coverage is only as good as your grep
        - label Silent landmine
          desc A missed site passes undefined; no error when you change the code
        - label Surfaces in production
          desc Crashes weeks later on a forgotten error path
    - label TypeScript
      children
        - label Whole-program check
          desc tsc enumerates every call site that no longer fits the contract
        - label All 23 light up at once
          desc Each stale call site becomes a compile error simultaneously
        - label Caught before it runs
          desc The incomplete refactor can't ship — red before users see it
theme
  palette #f43f5e #14b8a6
